SELECT define_provision($q$CGC_CITY_PLAN@2026-09-29$q$, $q$6.2.1.3 Table 6.2.1-1 RO1; Table 6.2.1-2 AO1$q$, 'ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT', $q$Setbacks are as follows: | Setback | Minimum distances measured in metres (m) | Front | 6m | Side and rear | Height | Setback | up to 4.5m | 1.5m | between 4.5m – 7.5m | 2m | exceeding 7.5m | an extra 0.5m is added for every 3m in height or part thereof over 7.5m | Between on-site habitable buildings (where not attached) | Double the applicable side setback. | OR$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Table 6.2.1-1 (Part A, ruleId 347) and Table 6.2.1-2 (Part B, ruleId 372)$q$, NULL, $q$Low density residential zone code (6.2.1)$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.goldcoast.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/37/0/false/08-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$Scheme definition 'Setback': shortest horizontal distance from the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the lot boundary. 'Outermost projection' excludes retractable blinds, fixed screens, rainwater fittings, ornamental attachments. Note: when acting as a QDC alternative provision, the building certifier may apply QDC/QHC measurement conventions (boundary clearance, also defined in Sch 1) - manual review.$q$, $q$gc_ldr_front_setback$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "CGC.gc_ldr_front_setback", "instrument_version": "CGC_CITY_PLAN@2026-09-29", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "6.2.1.3 Table 6.2.1-1 RO1; Table 6.2.1-2 AO1", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": 6, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2026-09-29", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "GOLD_COAST"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "CGC:LOW_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "gc_ldr_front_setback", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"front_setback_min\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": 6, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"applies where the small-lot or rear-lot alternatives are not used\"], \"exceptions\": [\"Dwelling houses on small lots: 4.5m to wall and balcony\", \"rear lots: 3m from all boundaries\"], \"formula_text\": null}\nLot conditions (not encoded): Standard (non-small-lot) table; small lot = lot area < 400m2 uses alternative table\nStructure scope 'all buildings (zone code setback table; no Class 10 distinction in standard table)' mapped by keyword to ['ANY']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES\nResearcher notes: Identical text in RO1 (accepted subject to requirements) and AO1 (assessable). Table 1.5-1 (s1.5 Building work regulated under the City Plan) lists 'Alternatives to QDC boundary clearance provisions' -> 'Buildings: Relevant zone code ...' (Section 33(2) BA). Applies to buildings (incl. Class 1 and Class 10a buildings). For 'Structures' only the Coastal erosion hazard and Road widening overlay codes are alternatives; 'QDC setbacks will apply to any building or structure where an alternative setback is not provided in the above codes.' Scheme refers to QDC MP1.1/MP1.2, not the QHC."}$q$::jsonb);
