SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "CGC.gc_ldr_small_lot_side_rear_setback", "instrument_version": "CGC_CITY_PLAN@2026-09-29", "topic": "SETBACK.SIDE", "title": "6.2.1.3 Table 6.2.1-1 RO1 (small lots); Table 6.2.1-2 AO1", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "BUILDING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_SIDE", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "Setbacks for Dwelling houses on small lots: | Setbacks | Minimum distances measured in metres (m) | Front | 4.5m to wall and balcony | Secondary frontage of corner lot | 4m (not including projections up to 2m) | Covered car parking (not applicable to the rear lane access) | 1m behind front wall or balcony; and 6m from the frontage where vehicles access the lot. | Side and rear (not applicable to the secondary frontage of corner lots) | Height | Setback | up to 4.5m | 1m to wall and balcony | 0.5m to outermost projection | 0m to class 10 buildings and/or non-habitable room where: - located along either a southern or western boundary; - a maximum length of 12m where no single part exceeds 6m in length - at least 1m separation from a habitable window of a neighbouring dwelling. | for the part between 4.5m - 7.5m | 1.5m to wall and balcony 1m to outermost projection | for that part exceeding 7.5m | 2m to wall and balcony 1.5m to outermost projection | Rear lane | 0.5m minimum 1m maximum for covered car parking | OR For development on rear lots the setback is 3m from all boundaries.", "extracted_value": null, "extracted_operator": "formula"}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "REFERRAL_TO_LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "effective_from": "2026-09-29", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "GOLD_COAST"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "CGC:LOW_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_1"], "sources": [{"key": "gc_ldr_small_lot_side_rear_setback", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"side_rear_setback_min_small_lot\", \"operator\": \"formula\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"up to 4.5m: 1m to wall and balcony; 0.5m to outermost projection\", \"part between 4.5m - 7.5m: 1.5m to wall and balcony; 1m to outermost projection\", \"part exceeding 7.5m: 2m to wall and balcony; 1.5m to outermost projection\"], \"exceptions\": [\"not applicable to the secondary frontage of corner lots\", \"0m to class 10 buildings and/or non-habitable room in stated circumstances\"], \"formula_text\": null}\nLot conditions (not encoded): small lot (< 400m2)\nStructure scope 'Dwelling house on small lot (wall/balcony vs outermost projection)' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES\nResearcher notes: Applies to side and rear. Table 1.5-1 (s1.5 Building work regulated under the City Plan) lists 'Alternatives to QDC boundary clearance provisions' -> 'Buildings: Relevant zone code ...' (Section 33(2) BA). Applies to buildings (incl. Class 1 and Class 10a buildings). For 'Structures' only the Coastal erosion hazard and Road widening overlay codes are alternatives; 'QDC setbacks will apply to any building or structure where an alternative setback is not provided in the above codes.' Scheme refers to QDC MP1.1/MP1.2, not the QHC."}$q$::jsonb);
